pairs.perturbed_problem:
Let $S=\left\{x \in(-\pi, \pi): x \neq 0, \pm \frac{\pi}{2}, \pm \frac{\pi}{3}\right\}$. The sum of all distinct solutions of the equation $\sqrt{3} \sec x+\operatorname{cosec} x+2(\tan x-\cot x)=0$ in the set $S$ is equal to

(A) -\frac{7\pi}{9}

(B) -\frac{2\pi}{9}

(C) 0

(D) \frac{5\pi}{9}
